  "note": "Design-time registry of contract packages: the one place a contract's id, path and package are declared together. Every Mycelium task reads it; the runner scripts find packages on disk; the repository check proves the two agree, both ways. Every field is read by code and no other field may appear (ContractRegistry refuses unknown fields). 'supersedes' names the contract this one replaces: a build may import one of the two, never both. 'provenance' is history for a reader (who a contract was written for, where it was promoted from): it is not checked and says nothing about the present. Which artifacts carry a contract today is in each artifact's own evidence manifest (META-INF/mycelium/evidence.json), not here. Status 'reference' means: pure reference implementation and rejection matrix exist; no game-target evidence is implied (DESIGN §11).",
